ow looking on the  bright side of life or anything along  those lines and you know he tells us  that genuine hope hope in the heart of  the one it inhabits and the judgments  cast upon it by someone who remains a  prisoner of objectivity genuine hope  can't be understood by some sort of  person like that because it straddles  the border between pure problems and  pure mystery he tells us that what hope  is he says to hope against all hope that  the person who I love will recover from  an illness that is devouring her and  which is considered to be incurable as  to say it is not possible that I am  alone in willing her recovery it is  impossible that reality and its very  depths as hospital only undifferenced to  what I declare to be a good in itself a  little later he gives you another really  wonderful characterization of hope as  thinking that there is something there  that will cooperate with you  being if it is what is ought to be now  you can frame that in terms of a problem  but what we're talking about there  really involves the very core of a human  being this is a mystery  it's affirming something meta  problematical something going beyond the  realm of the problems and the techniques  that can be used to resolve them one  last one that he mentions in there as  well is the meaning of the valley or the  mystery of the value of life and here we  have you know the typical philosophical  question right everybody shows up to  philosophy 101 or they hear that you're  a philosophy professor and they say oh  hey what's the meaning of life right as  if it's something that you could just  well it's 42 or it's have a lot of fun  or you know serve God or pick something  like that something that you could  encapsulate in a nice slogan if life was  just a problem yes you could do that or  perhaps it might be more complicated you  need a whole manual with lots and lots  of cases but it could be then just  turned into a set of you know procedures  to follow that's not the 